cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AUTOPHAGE: Bare-Metal Polymorphic x86-64 Galois-Field Genetic Engine with Six-Kernel Lean 4.35.0 Verification"
message: "If you use AUTOPHAGE, its Lean 4.35.0 proofs, or its companion white paper, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
version: "1.5.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/0thernes/autophage"
url: "https://0thernes.github.io/autophage/"
abstract: >-
  AUTOPHAGE v1.5.0 is a zero-dependency C11 bare-metal artificial-life and
  open-ended evolutionary engine in which 256-byte dual-strand organisms compile
  themselves via evolvable 8x8 F_2 ribosome matrices (VGF2P8AFFINEQB) into live
  native x86-64 RWX machine code with Galois-field polynomial recombination
  (PCLMULQDQ), 2x2 Cauchy MDS self-repair over GF(2^8), symplectic reversible
  Toffoli/Fredkin gates, POPCNT bit-erasure accounting, and 2-adic TZCNT
  kin-sensing. 56 Pure Lean 4.35.0 declarations (48 core/non-vacuity theorems
  including multi-step ledger heat-sink monotonicity T30 plus 8 adversarial
  false-variant refutations AT01-AT08; zero Mathlib, zero sorry in Solution,
  zero native_decide/bv_decide) about the Lean models in Spec.lean, not emitted
  x86-64 machine code, are verified by the Lean reference kernel plus 3
  independent Rust checkers locally on Windows and all 6 kernels with bubblewrap
  comparator + live negative tamper rejection in Ubuntu CI. Five theorems
  (T21, T23, T24, T28, T29) are elementary arithmetic or XOR helper lemmas, and
  the finite-field/reversible-gate facts are textbook results mechanically
  verified against this codebase's definitions. Engine behavior is tested by a
  19-gate falsification suite (including 6 planted negative mutants and B07
  ASan AVX-512 alignment regression Gate T19). Not peer-reviewed; resolves
  zero (0/1,900) overarching Mega-Atlas open problems.
